 "name_zh": "中国共产党一大•二大•四大纪念馆景区",
 "name_en": "Zhongguogongchandangyida•erda•sidajinianguan Scenic Area",
 "name_en_source": "pinyin",
 "slug": "zhongguogongchandangyida-erda-sidajinianguan-1443",
 "lat": 31.210884,
 "lon": 121.445075,
 "address_zh": "中共一大会址位于上海市兴业路76号、中共二大会址位于上海老成都北路7弄30号、中共四大纪念馆坐落于上海市虹口区四川北路绿地公园内",
 "address_en": "The site of the First Congress of the Communist Party of China is located at No. 76 Xingye Road, Shanghai. The site of the Second Congress of the Communist Party of China is located at No. 30, Lane 7, Old Chengdu North Road, Shanghai. The Memorial Hall of the Fourth National Congress of the Communist Party of China is located in the Greenland Park of Sichuan North Road, Hongkou District, Shanghai.",
 "address_en_source": "machine_translation",
 "category": "historic",
 "category_zh": "历史遗址",
 "category_en": "Historic site",
 "intro_zh": "中共“一大”原址是两栋砖木结构的两层石库门楼房，一栋是一大代表李汉俊的家宅，另一栋是一大代表在上海的住所--博文女校。中共“二大”会址是始建于1915年的石库门民居，曾是时任中央局宣传主任李达的寓所。中共“四大”原址于一二八事变中毁于战火，2006年异地重建了纪念馆，纪念馆由序厅、主展厅、影视厅和副展厅等组成。",
 "intro_en": "The original site of the \"National Congress\" of the Communist Party of China was two two-story Shikumen buildings with brick and wood structures. One was the home of Li Hanjun, the representative of the National Congress of the Communist Party of China, and the other was the residence of the National Congress of the Communist Party of China in Shanghai - Bowen Girls' School. The site of the Second National Congress of the Communist Party of China is a Shikumen residence built in 1915. It was once the residence of Li Da, the propaganda director of the Central Bureau. The original site of the \"Fourth National Congress\" of the Communist Party of China was destroyed by the war during the January 28th Incident. The memorial hall was rebuilt in 2006. The memorial hall consists of a preface hall, a main exhibition hall, a film and television hall and an auxiliary exhibition hall.",
 "intro_en_source": "machine_translation",
